WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:01.980
Living together?!

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:02.560
Yes.

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:05.540
I see. That might be a great idea.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.770
That instantly solves the problem!

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.830
I don't know if it'll work out,

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:14.230
but let's do our best 
to convince our parents!

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:15.990
Okay.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:51.420
09. True Feelings

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:51.670
So, what do you need to talk about?

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:55.510
It's about our move, actually...

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:59.940
I-I don't want to move.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:01.890
I want to stay here, even if it's by myself.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:06.190
My friend and I promised to reach a goal,

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:09.440
so I really want to continue 
being in the club with her.

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:10.910
I see...

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:13.900
But you know the transfer's 
already been decided,

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.420
and we can't afford to let you 
live on your own right now.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:21.300
On top of that, you're terrible at 
laundry and cooking for yourself, right?

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:24.670
I-I'll practice doing housework 
until spring comes,

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:27.410
and I have these documents 
about where I'll live!

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.370
Did you put these together yourself?

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:33.510
My friends helped me make it.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.670
New Life Proposal

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:36.340
They all came up with lots of ideas for me.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:36.340
Commuting to Hoshizaki High School 
From Our New Home Option

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:36.340
Living in the Konohata-san Home Option

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.050
Living in Mira-chan's home, huh?

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.530
That might sound sensible, but honestly,

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:46.470
from a parent's perspective, there's 
not enough thought put into it.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:49.690
You're forgetting the anxiety of leaving 
your child with another family.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:52.440
There are also the financial concerns.

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:57.070
<i>I knew it. As kids, there's nothing we can do...</i>

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:58.860
<i>No!</i>

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:00.360
<i>That's not right!</i>

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:04.490
<i>But in that case, why not act like a child 
should and try putting up at least some fight?</i>

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.470
I know I'm asking for a lot!

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:12.130
But I want to pursue my goal, 
my dream with Mira!

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:14.920
Please!

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:21.340
<i>I wonder how long it's been since 
she told us this much about herself.</i>

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.550
<i>We've made her put up with 
so much for a long time.</i>

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:31.610
Let's discuss this again 
when your father gets home.

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:35.020
But don't get your hopes up.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:36.680
Okay.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:37.930
Thank you.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:43.490
Oh, it's from Mira-chan's mother.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:45.530
<i>Mira told me what's going on.</i>

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:47.910
<i>We're open to discussing it anytime!</i>

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.160
<i>Let's talk it out!</i>

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.740
<i>I'll be waiting.</i>

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:51.960
They're so related...

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:54.800
<i>We'll have another discussion about it.</i>

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:55.630
So she says.

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:56.790
Thank goodness.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:59.120
I guess that means we've 
cleared the first hurdle.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.210
You've got a long road ahead of you, though.

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:03.260
Both of our families will need 
to discuss this together.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:06.420
Mira, you're getting ahead of yourself.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:11.350
Why did you agree to it so quickly, though?

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:13.320
Because it sounded fun!

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.210
Huh? Th-That's all?

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.340
I'm joking.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:21.000
It's a serious responsibility, 
so of course I'm worried,

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:24.360
but I want to support my children's dreams.

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:26.320
Thank you.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:29.960
I'm sure I'm not the only one, either.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.960
<b>Earth Sciences Club</b>

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:34.460
So, how'd it go?

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:35.510
Great!

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:38.620
Thanks to you all, both our 
families gave us the okay!

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:41.340
Thank you all so much for your help.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:42.540
Hooray!

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:43.670
We did it!

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:45.640
I'm so glad.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:48.890
I see. I guess I'm out of a role for now, then.

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:52.770
Oh? But Sakura-senpai, 
you were crying so much earlier.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.890
Shut up, newspaper club!

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:59.110
By the way, I think this whole 
chain of events was pretty dramatic,

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:02.670
so I'd love to print an article 
about it in the newspaper!

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:03.440
Huh?

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:06.790
I told her we shouldn't do 
anything crude like that...

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:07.670
What?!

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:12.130
Here I am, suggesting we cover something 
other than a scandal for once!

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:14.480
So, with that, I'd like to conduct 
an interview right away.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:15.270
Huh?

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:17.870
They both ran off at top speed.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:17.870
Huh? Huh?!

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:25.840
I'm sorry I didn't notice and acted so 
carefree while you agonized over this.

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:27.680
I should apologize.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:31.690
I kept it hidden from you because 
I didn't want to make you sad.

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:32.750
I'm sorry.

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:34.730
I should have talked to you about it sooner.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:38.880
I'll do my best to be more 
considerate from now on. So...

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:43.270
Yeah. I'll make sure to tell you how I feel, too.

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:50.940
Oh, we need to thank Suzu-chan, too.

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:51.830
Yeah.

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:55.540
Welcome.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:58.510
Huh? You seem down in the dumps.

00:05:58.510 --> 00:06:00.710
That's not true at all.

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:05.000
Is it because you're jealous 
Ao will get to use my sister's room?

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.760
I wouldn't be shaken up over that.

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:10.830
In fact, Ao living there now means

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:13.440
I can keep coming over to hang out and enjoy

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:16.320
the smell of Ao and Misa-nee at the same time!

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:20.560
Um, thank you for your help at the meeting.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:22.000
Thank you, Suzu-chan.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:25.580
It's fine. I didn't want to see Ao sad, after all.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:30.650
<i>Still, I can't believe Misa-nee's 
going to a university so far away.</i>

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:32.530
<i>I wish she had told me...</i>

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:34.120
Suzu-san?

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:35.730
Oh, sorry!

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:38.760
Anyway, let's celebrate 
your first step forward!

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:40.440
Take it all!

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.750
Triangle bikini pie?

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:46.380
It's a collection of designs 
that were rejected!

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:48.340
Thanks...

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:51.800
<i>No response...</i>

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:54.520
<i>Maybe she's busy?</i>

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:59.180
<i>Right. I'm sure she's preparing for college 
and handing over the student council.</i>

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:05.190
Good evening. Sorry for the late message. 
There's something I wanted to ask you about.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:03.940
Sakura-senpai?

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:08.120
Sorry to bother you during work.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:10.660
Not at all! I'm on my break, anyway.

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:14.680
I'm so happy to hear from you 
that I could break into a dance.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:17.040
Huh? What do you mean by that?

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:19.740
<i>She's still as unapproachable as ever.</i>

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:21.750
So, what did you want to discuss?

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:23.230
Oh, uh...

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:27.250
I was hoping you could teach me how 
to make Valentine's chocolates.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:30.650
What are you all silent for?

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:32.330
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:35.100
Uh, what kind of chocolate 
would you like to make?

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.280
Do you know what the person likes?

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:39.730
Well...

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:41.310
Enough for everyone?

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:42.710
How many are you dating?!

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:43.680
Huh?!

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:46.790
That's what you meant...

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:49.110
Friendship chocolate for the club members?

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:50.830
I thought you had a lover in mind.

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:53.390
Friendship chocolate is 
embarrassing enough.

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:55.410
I've never given anyone chocolate before.

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:57.170
Huh, I see.

00:07:57.170 --> 00:07:59.480
So you're a friendship chocolate virgin, then.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:04.160
I'll have to give you a tender, 
thorough lesson, then!

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:06.880
Couldn't you phrase it a bit more normally?

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:10.660
Okay, I'll message you the ingredients later.

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:11.670
Thanks.

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:14.280
If you need, I can buy your share, too.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:14.860
Huh?

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.600
You're giving some out, right?

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:18.920
Either friendship chocolate
or romantic chocolate?

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.880
I just keep getting shaken up today.

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:26.920
I let a bit of my real self slip out.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:30.610
Misa-nee!

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:32.880
<i>Sorry for the late reply.</i>

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:35.040
<i>I plan on moving toward the end of March.</i>

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:36.730
<i>I finished making arrangements today.</i>

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:39.950
Not only is it late, it's short, too.

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:44.010
<i>I guess we'll be saying farewell soon.</i>

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:47.070
<i>I've given her chocolates 
every year as a joke,</i>

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:48.700
<i>but what should I do this year?</i>

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:52.670
<b>Sakura-senpai</b>

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:52.670
<b>Valentine's Day</b>

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:51.120
Thanks for today.

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:52.670
Sure! Leave it to me!

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:56.110
Now, let's start by getting 
changed into this.

00:08:56.920 --> 00:08:57.540
Huh?

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:00.350
This is a major event for a maiden!

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:02.670
You should be more excited, 
more emotional about it!

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:03.730
I get it!

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:05.390
You're too close! You're scaring me!

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:07.850
First, we'll make chocolate in molds!

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:10.890
Huh? Don't you just cool 
those until they harden?

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:13.430
Non, non. You mustn't underestimate it.

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:17.070
It takes a lot of hard work to make 
delicious chocolates that melt in the mouth.

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:21.030
The key is the melting characteristics 
of the cocoa butter.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:24.610
You temper it, meaning you adjust the heat 
so it forms a uniform crystalline structure,

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:26.340
which gives you a glossy, soft chocolate

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:31.330
with a delicious, smooth, 
melt-in-your-mouth texture!

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:32.250
<i>I wonder if this what I sound 
like when I talk about rocks...</i>

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:32.840
First, we chop up the chocolate...

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:51.460
It's done!

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:54.230
Yeah! The shape and gloss are perfect.

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:55.610
Now we just decorate them a bit.

00:09:55.980 --> 00:09:58.080
Sorry it's basically as a taste test,

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:00.870
but would you accept my 
first friendship chocolate?

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:03.420
Of course!

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:07.470
It's delicious!

00:10:07.470 --> 00:10:08.530
Glad to hear it.

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:10.400
Senpai, you'd be very attractive

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:13.750
if you were more honest like that 
instead of being so standoffish.

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:15.840
You're one to talk, Suzu.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:18.660
You're always acting all excitable 
instead of showing your true feelings.

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:22.920
Honestly, we both suffer for it.

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:25.650
Well, what should I do next?

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:29.810
Happy Valentine's Day!

00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:34.520
You've done a lot for us, Senpai, 
so this is from both Mira and me.

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:36.280
This is from me, too.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:37.490
I have some for you, too.

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:39.160
Thank you so much!

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:40.450
You didn't have to, but thank you.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.150
Sakura-senpai, for you!

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:48.910
H-H-Happy... Valentine's Day!

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:53.780
I-I've only known you for a little while,

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:56.880
but it was fun enough,
so I wanted to thank you.

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:58.970
Thank you!

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:01.440
Wow!

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:02.930
Did you make them yourself?

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:04.560
I-I did.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:06.070
I had Suzu teach me.

00:11:06.070 --> 00:11:08.210
There are star chocolates and earth truffles.

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:10.950
I can't even bear to eat them!

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:13.190
Senpai, thank you.

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:18.770
They're handmade? 
It's like they're chocolates for your love!

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:22.780
They were delicious!

00:11:23.340 --> 00:11:25.770
Hey! Savor the taste a bit more!

00:11:25.770 --> 00:11:26.990
I put a lot of work into them!

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:28.410
They were delicious.

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:31.680
Well, whatever.

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:33.080
As long as they were good.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:36.990
<i>I wonder if she managed to give hers.</i>

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:44.100
Come in.

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:48.560
Hey, Suzu.

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:50.340
It feels like it's been a while.

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:53.340
I've been having trouble going 
through all the backed-up paperwork.

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:57.650
What is it?

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:04.230
Please accept my feelings.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.120
<b>Congratulations on Graduating!</b>

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:18.070
Monroe-senpai!

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:19.550
Congratulations on passing!

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:21.860
Thank you.

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:23.520
What are you looking at?

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:24.940
I'm searching for an apartment.

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:27.390
It'll be too far for me to commute from here.

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:28.780
I see.

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:34.300
I guess both you and Sakura-senpai will 
be going far away once you graduate.

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:36.650
Why are you making it sound so sad?

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:38.650
It's only two hours away by train.

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:39.830
<i>Graduation, huh?</i>

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:41.790
That's still so far.

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:41.790
<i>It's already been a year since then...</i>

00:12:41.790 --> 00:12:43.320
<i>It went by fast.</i>

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:45.740
Merging?

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:47.220
Starting in April.

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:49.200
Sorry the school's making you do this.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:50.680
That's so sudden!

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:52.280
I can't accept this!

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:55.360
They need to provide our 
club room and budget first!

00:12:55.360 --> 00:12:57.760
Morino-san, don't you have 
any opinion on this?

00:12:57.760 --> 00:12:58.960
Opinion?

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:03.060
I don't think we'll get along.

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:04.920
Are you picking a fight?

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:09.970
<i>I couldn't understand why 
Sakura-chan was so angry about it.</i>

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:12.570
<i>Merging, huh?</i>

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:13.930
<i>I never saw that coming,</i>

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:18.170
<i>but it might prove more beneficial 
on our college applications</i>

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:20.190
<i>if we get a proper club together.</i>

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:23.840
<b>Heaven</b>

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:22.740
Senpai, what's that?

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:27.380
It looks like our club activities and policies 
are completely different from Morino-san's,

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:26.800
<b>Earth</b>

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:29.360
so I thought it would be best 
to split into groups.

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:29.740
<b>Heaven</b>

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:29.740
<b>Earth</b>

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.860
Gosh, you really hate me, don't you?

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:34.960
You're the one who started it!

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:37.860
U-Um, let's get along...

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:41.800
<b>Man</b>

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:40.090
Inose, what are you doing?

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:45.630
Oh, uh, I thought I should
take a neutral stance...

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:45.630
<b>Heaven</b>

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:45.630
<b>Earth</b>

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:45.630
<b>Man</b>

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:51.200
<i>I suppose Sakura-chan noticed 
my matter-of-fact nature.</i>

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:55.430
<i>Afterward, we managed to 
get some new club members.</i>

00:13:55.840 --> 00:14:00.560
<i>They both had a big dream, 
something they could get lost in.</i>

00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:03.980
<i>My dream for the future was a long way off,</i>

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:08.960
<i>so I only ever thought of our 
club as a step toward that.</i>

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:11.780
<i>I'm jealous.</i>

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:17.870
<i>No, my role as president is to make 
sure the club runs properly.</i>

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:22.730
<i>I need to manage our schedule,
 take photos for the newsletter, edit it,</i>

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:24.400
<i>and guide the younger members.</i>

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:26.650
<i>But taking a step back to look at it all...</i>

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:29.780
<i>Is that fun?</i>

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:31.850
Senpai.

00:14:32.590 --> 00:14:35.080
Senpai? Monroe-senpai?

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:37.670
Oh, sorry. What is it?

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:41.990
I was hoping we could all take a group 
photo after the graduation ceremony.

00:14:41.990 --> 00:14:42.810
That sounds nice.

00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:45.650
Shall we take it outside 
the club building, then?

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:46.640
Yeah!

00:14:46.640 --> 00:14:48.110
We're looking forward to it.

00:14:48.680 --> 00:14:51.850
<i>To think this would bother me 
now, after all this time...</i>

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:54.330
<b>Hoshizaki Public High School
 Graduation Ceremony Hall</b>

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:57.600
Congratulations on graduating!

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:01.110
It's so sad saying goodbye to you two!

00:15:01.110 --> 00:15:03.840
It's nothing to cry that much over.

00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:07.370
Senpai, your handkerchief's all wet.

00:15:07.930 --> 00:15:09.760
Wrong one! Use these!

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:13.050
Looks like the camera's set right.

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:16.530
That's because you taught me so well, Senpai.

00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:20.030
I'll do my best to take good 
pictures from now on, too.

00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:21.020
Please do.

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:24.010
You forgot one thing, though.

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:26.880
The memory card's not in it.

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:30.750
Mira, you should do it now.

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:31.280
Yeah.

00:15:32.310 --> 00:15:34.460
Monroe-senpai, Sakura-senpai!

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:37.760
This is to commemorate your graduation!

00:15:38.440 --> 00:15:39.700
Thanks.

00:15:42.440 --> 00:15:45.440
It's the model of the moon we 
made for the cultural festival.

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:49.020
I was hoping I could draw 
a few more craters on it.

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:50.800
It wasn't finished?

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:54.010
Is this a miniature boring core?

00:15:54.740 --> 00:15:57.970
It's full of the dirt we extracted together!

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:03.600
Also, here. We added more pages 
to the album we were given.

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:06.020
Pictures of me?

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:06.950
Yes!

00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:11.400
You weren't in many photos since you 
were always in charge of taking them,

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:14.240
so we collected photos from everyone!

00:16:17.770 --> 00:16:18.660
<i>I...</i>

00:16:19.570 --> 00:16:22.020
<i>was smiling this much?</i>

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:24.820
Thank you.

00:16:25.820 --> 00:16:28.590
All that's left is to add today's 
photo, and it's complete!

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:31.070
Sorry I'm late!

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:32.810
Sensei, hurry!

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:36.720
I'll set the timer for ten seconds, okay?

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:39.180
Ino! Blow your nose first!

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:45.270
Five, four, three, two, one...

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:54.360
I'm glad they were able
 to see us off with smiles.

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.490
Ino was a mess, though.

00:16:57.280 --> 00:17:02.220
We had our share of troubles, 
but the club was pretty fun, wasn't it?

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:03.710
Yeah.

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:09.040
It looks I was able to actually enjoy it, too.

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:10.900
Actually?

00:17:11.770 --> 00:17:12.760
Wait, what?!

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:14.060
What's the matter?!

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:20.860
You couldn't figure out whether 
you actually enjoyed the club?

00:17:21.990 --> 00:17:24.350
You get too serious 
about the strangest things.

00:17:25.430 --> 00:17:31.650
Once April comes, don't worry about anything.
Just enjoy college life to the fullest.

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:35.420
I'll be right there with you, after all.

00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:39.780
Yeah.

00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:44.020
Once we're in college, 
will you join me for mixers?

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:47.200
Huh?! You're interested in those?

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:49.960
I just want to see you flustered.

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:54.670
<i>During spring break, Ao moved into my house.</i>

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:58.260
Okay, all done bringing the stuff in!

00:17:58.260 --> 00:18:00.510
Thanks. I can handle the rest myself.

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:03.260
No need! I'll help you unpack.

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:04.580
Huh? Hey, wait!

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:07.190
We're going to be living together now.

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:11.270
<b>To Mira</b>

00:18:08.070 --> 00:18:09.410
"To Mira"?

00:18:09.410 --> 00:18:11.270
Is this for me?

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:13.780
Hey, can I open...

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:18.820
Y-Y-You can't open it!

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:24.580
What's the matter, you two? You're frowning.

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:28.130
A fight between two astronomy lovers, huh?

00:18:28.570 --> 00:18:29.670
It's most likely because...

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:30.900
That Mira!

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:35.000
I told her the moon was formed 
from a comet that struck Earth.

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:36.980
The Giant Impact Hypothesis.

00:18:37.900 --> 00:18:40.110
Ao has no sense of romance.

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:44.720
Some people believe the moon came flying 
in and got caught by the Earth's gravity.

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:46.270
The Capture Hypothesis.

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:48.110
That's what I think.

00:18:48.110 --> 00:18:50.560
Your mother votes for Ao-chan's idea!

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:52.480
That's not what this is about!

00:18:53.470 --> 00:18:56.440
I see. Mira started going 
through your luggage?

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:57.860
Sorry about that.

00:18:57.860 --> 00:19:01.310
It's okay. I shouldn't have shouted, either.

00:19:01.310 --> 00:19:04.070
I'm so happy to be living in the same home,

00:19:04.070 --> 00:19:06.190
but if this how our first day goes...

00:19:06.850 --> 00:19:08.890
It's only natural you'd be worried.

00:19:09.970 --> 00:19:13.140
You grew up in different environments, 
and now you're living together.

00:19:13.140 --> 00:19:16.160
I'm sure all kinds of things 
will come up between you.

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:20.280
Besides, if you're feeling that way,
then I'm sure Mira is, too.

00:19:21.530 --> 00:19:25.490
I'm talking like I know it all, 
but I'm worried about my new life, too.

00:19:25.490 --> 00:19:26.870
Especially the housework.

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:29.590
I'm just not very good at laundry or cooking.

00:19:29.590 --> 00:19:31.920
<i>Suddenly, I feel much closer to her.</i>

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:34.590
By the way, Ao-kun.

00:19:34.590 --> 00:19:37.010
Sorry to ask, but could 
you do something for me?

00:19:37.010 --> 00:19:38.420
Something for you?

00:19:38.420 --> 00:19:41.640
If you could water the plants 
on this shrine every morning

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:44.030
and clean it sometimes, I'd be grateful.

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:45.070
Sure.

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:48.020
One more thing.

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:52.280
Mira, I'm coming in.

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:54.340
I'm sorry about earlier.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:58.670
Ao! I'm sorry!

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:02.080
Wow, a constellation print...

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:03.050
It's so cute.

00:20:03.540 --> 00:20:07.500
I was actually planning to give it to you 
when I said goodbye before moving,

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:10.520
but now we can start using them together.

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:12.980
I'm looking forward to being here.

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:21.750
I won't go through your things anymore!

00:20:21.750 --> 00:20:22.850
Also...

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:25.780
I support the Giant Impact Hypothesis, too!

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:27.130
<i>She was concerned about that...</i>

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:31.280
This feels so good.

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:34.090
Ao, I made some coffee.

00:20:34.090 --> 00:20:35.040
Thanks.

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:36.890
Oh, look, look!

00:20:36.890 --> 00:20:38.330
Venus is out!

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:39.990
It's hard to see since it's so low,

00:20:39.990 --> 00:20:42.010
but maybe Mercury's nearby.

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:45.170
They said it'll be easiest to spot next week.

00:20:45.170 --> 00:20:47.260
The greatest eastern elongation, right?

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:49.920
It'll be visible since it's 
furthest from the sun, yeah?

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:54.180
I've grown a bit too, haven't I?

00:20:57.520 --> 00:21:00.810
We were both looking at 
different stars last year, and now...

00:21:00.810 --> 00:21:02.080
It's kind of weird.

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:03.580
Yeah.

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:08.620
<i>Please take care of Mira while I'm gone.</i>

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:14.260
Are you all right?!

00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:16.280
How many sugars are in this?

00:21:16.280 --> 00:21:21.500
Sorry. I didn't know how you like it,
 so I put five in...

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:23.260
That wasn't enough, was it?

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:25.600
Please give it to me black.

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:32.220
Nice to meet all of you new students!

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:34.430
<b>Passionately
 Welcoming
 Earth Sciences Club 
New Members</b>

00:21:32.510 --> 00:21:34.430
We're the earth sciences club!

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:40.620
Would you like to chase the 
stars or crack rocks with us?

00:21:40.620 --> 00:21:41.890
If any of you are interested,

00:21:41.890 --> 00:21:43.670
please come to the cultural 
club building after school!

00:21:42.990 --> 00:21:45.060
M-Mira-chan, no!

00:21:45.060 --> 00:21:47.860
We have to get permission to recruit!

00:21:48.210 --> 00:21:51.830
New students, we are the earth sciences club!

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:53.200
Wait! Please wait!

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:54.290
That's...

00:21:54.890 --> 00:21:56.040
The earth sciences club?

00:21:57.660 --> 00:21:59.400
<i>Today is the start of my second year!</i>

00:21:59.400 --> 00:22:01.970
<i>I wonder if I'll have kouhai, too.</i>

00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:03.410
<i>I wonder what they'll be like.</i>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
10. 
Rain With Occasional Fortune Telling

00:23:35.980 --> 00:23:39.350
Next time, "Rain With 
Occasional Fortune Telling."
